{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2001","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Longest Max Min Subsequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer sequence $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$. Let $$$S$$$ be the set of all possible non-empty subsequences of $$$a$$$ without duplicate elements. Your goal is to find the longest sequence in $$$S$$$. If there are multiple of them, find the one that minimizes lexicographical order after multiplying terms at odd positions by $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, given $$$a = [3, 2, 3, 1]$$$, $$$S = \\{[1], [2], [3], [2, 1], [2, 3], [3, 1], [3, 2], [2, 3, 1], [3, 2, 1]\\}$$$. Then $$$[2, 3, 1]$$$ and $$$[3, 2, 1]$$$ would be the longest, and $$$[3, 2, 1]$$$ would be the answer since $$$[-3, 2, -1]$$$ is lexicographically smaller than $$$[-2, 3, -1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A sequence $$$c$$$ is a subsequence of a sequence $$$d$$$ if $$$c$$$ can be obtained from $$$d$$$ by the deletion of several (possibly, zero or all) elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A sequence $$$c$$$ is lexicographically smaller than a sequence $$$d$$$ if and only if one of the following holds:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$c$$$ is a prefix of $$$d$$$, but $$$c \\ne d$$$;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" in the first position where $$$c$$$ and $$$d$$$ differ, the sequence $$$c$$$ has a smaller element than the corresponding element in $$$d$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 5 \\cdot 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 3 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le n$$$) — the sequence $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$3 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output the answer in the following format:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output an integer $$$m$$$ in the first line — the length of $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then output $$$m$$$ integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_m$$$ in the second line — the sequence $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n4\n3 2 1 3\n4\n1 1 1 1\n9\n3 2 1 3 2 1 3 2 1\n1\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3 2 1\n1\n1\n3\n3 1 2\n1\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n2\n1 2\n10\n5 2 1 7 9 7 2 5 5 2\n2\n1 2\n10\n2 2 8 7 7 9 8 1 9 6\n9\n9 1 7 5 8 5 6 4 1\n3\n3 3 3\n6\n1 6 4 4 6 5\n6\n3 4 4 5 3 3\n10\n4 1 4 5 4 5 10 1 5 1\n7\n1 2 1 3 2 4 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1 2\n5\n5 1 9 7 2\n2\n1 2\n6\n2 7 9 8 1 6\n7\n9 1 7 5 8 6 4\n1\n3\n4\n1 4 6 5\n3\n4 5 3\n4\n5 4 10 1\n5\n2 1 3 4 6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, $$$S = \\{[1], [2], [3], [1, 3], [2, 1], [2, 3], [3, 1], [3, 2], [2, 1, 3], [3, 2, 1]\\}$$$. Among them, $$$[2, 1, 3]$$$ and $$$[3, 2, 1]$$$ are the longest and $$$[-3, 2, -1]$$$ is lexicographical smaller than $$$[-2, 1, -3]$$$, so $$$[3, 2, 1]$$$ is the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, $$$S = \\{[1]\\}$$$, so $$$[1]$$$ is the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"2001D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2001/problem/D"}